# BaseX itself. Everything under basex/ is either the downloaded distribution or a
# REPRODUCIBLE build product (data/ alone is 2.8 GB on a built corpus), with three
# exceptions that must ship: the jar we run, the licence that permits us to ship
# it, and the home marker.
#
# BaseX is BSD-3-Clause, so redistributing BaseX.jar IS permitted, provided the
# copyright notice travels with it -- which is why basex/LICENSE is not optional.
# (An earlier version of this file claimed redistribution was not permitted. That
# was simply false, and it is why the jar went unshipped for months.)
#
# .basexhome is a 0-byte upstream marker and it is LOAD-BEARING. MEASURED both
# directions 2026-08-25, same jar, same command: with it, CREATE DB writes to
# basex/data; without it BaseX relocates its whole home to $HOME/basex, builds
# there successfully, and every check in this directory then reports the database
# as never built. The build succeeds and the tool says it did not.
#
# ⚠ NOTE THE FORM. `basex/` plus `!basex/BaseX.jar` ships NOTHING: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded. It must be `basex/*`.
# Proven by execution in a throwaway repo -- form A staged nothing, form B staged
# exactly the three files below.
basex/*
!basex/BaseX.jar
!basex/LICENSE
!basex/.basexhome

# BaseX writes its own `.basex` config on first run, into whichever directory it
# resolved as home, and it records absolute paths. The rule above already covers
# basex/.basex; this covers a home that resolves anywhere else in the tree.
.basex

# Transient build products. The serialized effective tree is discarded by
# build-effective.sh unless KEEP_EFF=1; the manifest beside it is the durable part.
_eff/tree/
_stage/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build MANIFESTS. Regenerated by every build, and they record absolute paths
# (`out`, `staging_dir`) — i.e. committing them would leak a username, the exact
# defect the path-resolution fix in this same commit removes from the scripts.
_eff/effective-manifest.json
stage-manifest.json
